# INJECTED DEFECT -- NEVER APPLY TO A SHIPPING BUILD.
#
# One microframe in every 100 frames carries 832 B against the witness
# endpoint's advertised wMaxPacketSize of 800 B, to make R4a fire on
# hardware. alt_mps_hs is overridden to 1024 because itd_fill_out refuses
# len > max_packet and the descriptor could not otherwise be built.
#
# TWO FINDINGS FROM BUILDING THIS, both recorded because they were both
# predicted wrong (2026-08-05):
#
# 1. R4a IS reachable on this bench. The prediction was that a packet beyond
#    wMaxPacketSize is a babble condition XUD would refuse before lib_xua's
#    decoupler could count it, making R4a unprovable here. False: an
#    aggressive first version (832 B every frame) put 832 straight into the
#    device's size histogram -- sizes came back [160, 192, 832]. The device
#    stack accepts and counts it.
#
# 2. But that version never reached R4a, because the judge's
#    manifest-contradiction guard fired first: the mean packet size was 1.93x
#    the declared prediction, and a mis-declared format and an oversizing
#    host are indistinguishable in the mean, so the report was invalidated
#    wholesale. The guard is right to do that -- it exists so a wrong
#    manifest cannot produce a cited FAIL against a conformant host -- but it
#    means R4a can only rule on oversize that is RARE or SMALL enough to
#    leave the mean inside one audio frame of the prediction. That
#    interaction between two safety mechanisms is worth knowing about.
#
# Hence this version: rare (1 frame in 100) and rate-neutral (832 + three
# normal microframes ~= 1408 B against a nominal 1411), so the mean moves by
# under 1 B and R4a gets to speak. 832 is 26 whole 32 B audio frames, so R4b
# stays clean and only the size rule has cause to fire.
#
# Apply:  git apply tools/uacvalidate/defects/r4a-oversize.patch
# Revert: git checkout -- usb_audio.cpp
